---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import { componentsSidebar } from '../../data/nav';
---
<ArticleLayout
  title="Components"
  section="components"
  description="Reusable, accessible parts of the user interface, with live examples and code."
  pageTitle="Components"
  pageSubtitle="Reusable parts of the user interface, with live examples and code."
  sidebarGroups={componentsSidebar}
  sidebarLabel="Components"
>
  <div class="govbb-prose">
    <p>
      Components are reusable parts of the user interface. Each component page shows a
      live preview and the code you can copy.
    </p>
    <p>
      More components are being migrated into the system. For now the code panel shows
      HTML and CSS; web component and React versions will follow.
    </p>
    <h2>Available components</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/components/button/">Button</a> — help users carry out an action.</li>
      <li>
        <a href="/components/error-summary/">Error Summary</a> — summarise form errors
        at the top of the page.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/components/show-hide/">Show/Hide</a> — reveal secondary content on demand.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</ArticleLayout>
